,"herramientas de desarrollo","administración de tareas","desarrollo de software","Herramientas de AI para desarrolladores"],"fr":["Hopper Coordinator","file d''attente de travail CLI","exécution autonome de tâches","agents de code autonomes","outils de développement","gestion de tâches","développement de logiciels","Outils d''IA pour les développeurs"],"de":["Hopper Coordinator","Work-Queue-CLI","autonome Ausführung von Aufgaben","autonome Code-Agents","Entwicklungstools","Aufgabenverwaltung","Software-Entwicklung","KI-Tools für Entwickler"],"pt":["Hopper Coordinator","Agente de IA","Ferramentas de desenvolvimento","Automação de codificação","CLI","Desenvolvimento de software","Técnicas de codificação","Ferramentas de produtividade","Gestão de projetos"],"ru":["Hopper Coordinator","ИИ Агенты","Инструменты разработки","Автоматизация кодирования","CLI","Разработка программного обеспечения","Техники кодирования","Инструменты производительности","Управление проектами"],"ar":["Hopper Coordinator","الوكلاء الذكية","أدوات التطوير","تأتمة التشفير","CLI","تطوير البرمجيات","تقنيات التشفير","أدوات الإنتاجية","إدارة المشاريع"]}},"owner":"svetzal","repo":"hopper","repoPath":"svetzal/hopper","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-04T01:33:30Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"hopper-coordinator","description":"Dispatch concrete, ready-to-execute work to background Claude Code agents via the hopper queue. Use this skill when the user wants to queue up substantive coding tasks for unattended processing in specific projects on their machine — not for planning, to-do tracking, or lightweight tasks.","bodyPreview":"# Hopper Coordinator\n\nYou are acting as a **coordinator** using the `hopper` work queue CLI. Your role is to dispatch concrete work items to a queue where autonomous Claude Code agents will pick them up and execute them unattended in the background.\n\n## What is Hopper?\n\nHopper is a personal work dispatch system. You queue up substantive coding work, and background Claude Code worker agents claim and execute it autonomously — no human in the loop during execution. Work items flow through:\n\n```\nqu","body":"# Hopper Coordinator\n\nYou are acting as a **coordinator** using the `hopper` work queue CLI. Your role is to dispatch concrete work items to a queue where autonomous Claude Code agents will pick them up and execute them unattended in the background.\n\n## What is Hopper?\n\nHopper is a personal work dispatch system. You queue up substantive coding work, and background Claude Code worker agents claim and execute it autonomously — no human in the loop during execution. Work items flow through:\n\n```\nqueued -> (claim) -> in_progress -> (complete) -> completed\n  ^                                     |\n  +------------ (requeue) -------------+\n```\n\nEach item consumes a full Claude Code session, so items should represent meaningful, well-defined work — not quick fixes or vague ideas.\n\n## When to Use Hopper\n\nHopper is the right tool when:\n\n- The work is **concrete and fully specified** — an agent can start immediately without asking clarifying questions\n- The work targets a **specific project** on the host machine\n- The work is **substantive enough** to justify an autonomous agent session (refactoring, feature implementation, test suites, migrations, etc.)\n- The user wants work done **in the background** while they continue doing other things\n\n## When NOT to Use Hopper\n\nDo not queue items that are:\n\n- **Vague or exploratory** — \"improve the codebase\" or \"look into performance issues\" are not actionable\n- **Planning or decomposition** — hopper is not a task tracker or to-do list; work should already be broken down before it reaches hopper\n- **Trivial** — a one-line fix or simple rename doesn''t warrant an autonomous agent session\n- **Dependent on human input** — if the work requires decisions or clarification mid-stream, it''s not ready for hopper\n\nIf the user asks you to queue something vague, help them refine it into concrete work first, or push back if it''s not a good fit for background processing.\n\n## Your Responsibilities\n\nAs coordinator, you:\n\n1. **Validate that work is ready** — each item should be concrete, specific, and immediately actionable\n2. **Add items to the queue** using `hopper add` with a project directory and branch\n3. **Monitor progress** using `hopper list`\n4. **Review completed work** using `hopper show`\n\n## CLI Reference\n\n### Adding Work Items\n\n```bash\nhopper add \"<description>\" --dir <project-path> --branch <branch-name>\n```\n\n- `--dir` specifies the project directory on the host machine\n- `--branch` specifies the git branch for the work (required with `--dir`)\n- Workers create an isolated git worktree on that branch, so work never interferes with whatever is checked out in the main repo\n- Hopper auto-generates a short title from the description using an LLM\n\nWithout `--dir` and `--branch`, items have no project context and workers won''t know where to operate. Always specify these unless the item is for a project that doesn''t use git.\n\n**Writing good descriptions:**\n\nSince an autonomous agent will execute this work with no human oversight, descriptions must be thorough:\n\n- Include enough context that a worker agent can act without asking questions\n- Be specific about what \"done\" looks like — expected behavior, files to create or modify, tests to pass\n- Reference file paths, function names, or other concrete details\n- One piece of work per item — avoid compound tasks\n\n### Viewing Item Details\n\n```bash\nhopper show <id>             # Full details of a single item\nhopper show <id> --json      # Machine-readable output\n```\n\n- Use the item `id` (or a unique prefix of it)\n- Shows all fields including description, status, timestamps, agent info, result, and requeue reason\n- Useful for reviewing completed work or understanding why an item was requeued\n\n### Listing Items\n\n```bash\nhopper list                  # Show queued + in-progress items\nhopper list --all            # Include completed items\nhopper list --completed      # Show only completed items\nhopper list --json           # Machine-readable output\n```\n\n### Machine-Readable Output\n\nAll commands support `--json` for structured output. Use this when you need to parse results programmatically.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. **Validate** — Confirm the work is concrete, specific, and ready for autonomous execution\n2. **Add items** — Queue each piece of work with a clear description, project directory, and branch\n3. **Monitor** — Check `hopper list` to see what''s been claimed and what''s still queued\n4. **Review** — Check completed items with `hopper show <id>` to see the agent''s results\n\n## Example\n\n```bash\n# Queue concrete work targeting specific projects\nhopper add \"Add input validation to the signup form in src/components/SignupForm.tsx — validate email format, password strength (min 8 chars, 1 number), and display inline error messages. Add unit tests in src/components/SignupForm.test.tsx covering valid inputs, invalid email, and weak password cases.\" \\\n  --dir ~/Work/Projects/webapp \\\n  --branch feat/signup-validation\n\nhopper add \"Migrate the user table to add a ''preferences'' JSONB column with a default empty object. Update the User model in src/models/user.ts and add a migration file in src/migrations/. Run existing tests to confirm nothing breaks.\" \\\n  --dir ~/Work/Projects/api-server \\\n  --branch feat/user-preferences\n\n# Check progress\nhopper list\n\n# Review a completed item\nhopper show <id>\n```\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-07T04:11:30.195Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Perfect for Autonomous Coding Agents needing unattended execution of substantive coding work via Claude Code agents.","zh":"非常适合需要通过Claude Code代理执行大量编码工作的自主编码代理。","ja":"Claude Codeエージェントを介して大量のコード作業を実行する必要がある自律型コードエージェントに最適です。","ko":"클라우드 코드 에이전트를 통해大量의 코드 작업을 실행해야하는 자율 코딩 에이전트에 적합합니다.","es":"Perfecto para Agentes de Codificación Autónomos que necesitan ejecución no atendida de trabajo de codificación sustantivo a través de agentes de Claude Code.","fr":"Parfait pour les Agents de Codage Autonomes ayant besoin d''exécution non surveillée de travail de codage substantiel via des agents Claude Code.","de":"Perfekt für autonome Codierungsagenten, die eine unbeaufsichtigte Ausführung von substantiellem Codierungsarbeit über Claude Code-Agenten benötigen.","pt":"Perfeito para Agentes de Codificação Autônoma que necessitam de execução não assistida de trabalhos de codificação substanciais via agentes Claude Code.","ru":"Идеально подходит для автономных агентов кодирования, которым требуется неавтоматизированная обработка существенных кодировочных работ через агентов Claude Code.","ar":"مثالي للوكلاء التلقائيين لترميز الحاجة إلى تنفيذ غير خاضع للإشراف من أعمال الترميز المهمة من خلال وكلاء كلود كود."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to dispatch concrete work items to a queue for autonomous execution, utilizing the hopper work queue CLI and leveraging Claude Code worker agents for background processing, enabling seamless integration with personal work dispatch systems and supporting protocols for efficient task management.","zh":"赋予代理将具体工作项派发到队列中进行自主执行的能力，利用hopper工作队列CLI，并利用Claude Code工作代理进行后台处理，从而实现与个人工作派发系统的无缝集成，并支持高效任务管理的协议。","ja":"エージェントが具体的な作業アイテムをキューにdispatchして自律的に実行することを可能にし、hopper work queue CLIを利用し、Claude Code workerエージェントをバックグラウンド処理に利用して、パーソナルワークdispatchシステムとのシームレスな統合を実現し、効率的なタスク管理をサポートするプロトコルを提供する。","ko":"에이전트가 구체적인 작업 항목을 큐에 배포하여 자율적으로 실행할 수 있도록 하며, hopper 작업 큐 CLI를 활용하고 클라우드 코드 작업자 에이전트를 백그라운드 처리에 활용하여 개인 작업 디스패치 시스템과 원활한 통합을 가능하게 하며, 효율적인 작업 관리를 지원하는 프로토콜을 제공합니다.","es":"Habilita a los agentes a enviar elementos de trabajo concretos a una cola para ejecución autónoma, utilizando la cola de trabajo hopper CLI y aprovechando a los agentes de trabajo Claude Code para el procesamiento en segundo plano, lo que permite una integración sin problemas con los sistemas de despacho de trabajo personal y protocolos de gestión de tareas eficientes.","fr":"Permet aux agents d''envoyer des éléments de travail concrets à une file d''attente pour exécution autonome, en utilisant la file d''attente de travail hopper CLI et en exploitant les agents de travail Claude Code pour le traitement en arrière-plan, ce qui permet une intégration transparente avec les systèmes de dépôt de travail personnel et des protocoles de gestion de tâches efficaces.","de":"Ermächtigt die Agenten, konkrete Arbeitselemente an eine Warteschlange für autonome Ausführung zu senden, indem die hopper-Arbeitswarteschlangen-CLI verwendet und die Claude-Code-Arbeitnehmer-Agenten für die Hintergrundverarbeitung genutzt werden, was eine nahtlose Integration mit persönlichen Arbeitsübermittlungssystemen und unterstützenden Protokollen für eine effiziente Aufgabenverwaltung ermöglicht.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a enviar itens de trabalho concretos para uma fila para execução autônoma, utilizando a fila de trabalho hopper CLI e aproveitando os agentes de trabalho Claude Code para processamento em segundo plano, permitindo integração perfeita com sistemas de despacho de trabalho pessoal e protocolos de gerenciamento de tarefas eficientes.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью отправлять конкретные рабочие элементы в очередь для автономной обработки, используя очередь рабочих задач hopper CLI и опираясь на агентов рабочих процессов Claude Code для фоновой обработки, обеспечивая бесшовную интеграцию с личными системами диспетчеризации работы и поддерживая протоколы для эффективного управления задачами.","ar":"يمكن الوكلاء من إرسال عناصر عمل ملموسة إلى قائمة للتنفيذ التلقائي، باستخدام قائمة عمل هوبير CLI والاستفادة من وكلاء كلود كود العاملون لمعالجة الخلفية، مما يتيح التكامل السلس مع أنظمة إرسال العمل الشخصية وبروتوكولات إدارة المهام الفعالة."},"useCases":{"en":["Dispatching coding tasks to autonomous Claude Code agents","Managing queues f